{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I'm Dr. Lee, one of your oncology team members. You're here for your 20th cycle of high-dose methotrexate. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’m doing okay. I’ve been feeling pretty stable since my last treatment. No headaches or weakness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. We’ll be giving the methotrexate tonight, starting around 11 PM. Before that, we’ll start IV fluids to help protect your kidneys and keep your urine alkaline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Last time I had some nausea with Zofran. Is that still the plan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Actually, we’re switching to fosaprepitant this time. It tends to work better and causes fewer headaches than Zofran. We hope it helps you feel even better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that sounds good. I really didn’t like those headaches."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:09:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor your urine pH closely to make sure it stays above 8.5. That helps the methotrexate clear safely from your body."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And when does the leucovorin start?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "About 24 hours after the methotrexate finishes. It helps protect your healthy cells from the chemo. We’ll give it through your port."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. My foot pain has been acting up a bit. Can I still take my gabapentin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:15:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, absolutely. Gabapentin is safe to continue. You can also use oxycodone as needed for breakthrough pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. And my asthma inhalers—I’ve been using them as usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:18:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, keep using your albuterol and the combination inhaler as prescribed. Your breathing sounds clear today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve also been on citalopram for my mood. It’s been helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:21:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important to maintain. We’ll keep it on your list. Any feelings of low mood or anxiety lately?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not really. I’ve been feeling pretty steady."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2176-07-05 08:24:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Glad to hear it. We’ll check your labs regularly to monitor your blood counts and kidney function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2176-07-05 23:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re about to start the methotrexate infusion now. It’ll run for about two hours. Let us know if you feel any discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2176-07-05 23:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready. No issues so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2176-07-06 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. The infusion went smoothly. Your urine pH has stayed above 8.5, which is perfect."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2176-07-06 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I haven’t felt nauseous at all—maybe the fosaprepitant is working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2176-07-06 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. We’ll draw your first methotrexate level later today to track how it’s clearing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2176-07-06 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had an MRI this morning, right? Was everything okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2176-07-06 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the MRI showed no signs of lymphoma recurrence. The changes in your brain are stable, which is exactly what we want to see."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2176-07-06 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s such a relief. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2176-07-06 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also saw some chronic sinus inflammation, but nothing new or concerning. It’s unrelated to your lymphoma."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2176-07-06 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had sinus issues for years. Nothing to worry about, I hope."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2176-07-06 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it’s not related to your treatment. We’ll leave it to your primary doctor unless it flares up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2176-07-06 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your methotrexate level came back at 0.17 micromolar. That’s declining well, so we’re on track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2176-07-06 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that a safe level?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2176-07-06 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s low enough that we can safely continue with leucovorin and IV fluids for a bit longer and plan for discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2176-07-06 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Will I need to take leucovorin at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2176-07-06 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, because your level is clearing so well, you won’t need oral leucovorin or bicarbonate after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2176-07-06 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s one less thing to manage. What about aspirin? I was off it last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2176-07-06 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We held it during your stay for safety, but you’ll restart it at home. We used heparin for clot prevention while you were here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2176-07-06 14:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, because of my history with blood clots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2176-07-06 14:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We always take extra precautions with that. Your leg has no swelling, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2176-07-07 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re cleared to go home today. You tolerated everything very well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2176-07-07 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s wonderful. No more IVs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2176-07-07 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, we’ll remove the IV before you leave. Just continue your regular meds, including aspirin, citalopram, gabapentin, and your inhalers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2176-07-07 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll keep using oxycodone if my foot pain flares up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2176-07-07 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, as needed. And call us if you have any fever, unusual fatigue, or signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2176-07-07 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thank you for explaining everything so clearly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2176-07-07 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. You’re doing well with your treatment. We’ll see you for your next cycle in a few weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2176-07-07 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be ready. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2176-07-07 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Have a safe trip home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2176-07-05 00:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2176-07-07 19:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old woman with primary central nervous system lymphoma was admitted for her 20th cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy. She reported feeling well with no neurological symptoms or systemic complaints. The chemotherapy was administered without complications, and she experienced excellent nausea control with fosaprepitant instead of her prior antiemetic. Urine alkalinization was maintained throughout, and her methotrexate level at 30 hours was 0.17 uM, indicating safe clearance. A brain MRI showed no evidence of lymphoma recurrence, with only stable chronic changes. She remained stable neurologically and hematologically, with no signs of infection or thrombosis. Aspirin was held during admission and restarted at discharge, with heparin bridging for DVT prophylaxis. She was discharged home in stable condition with no need for post-discharge leucovorin or bicarbonate, continuing her regular medications including those for chronic pain, asthma, and depression.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Primary central nervous system lymphoma, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Pain in limb",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Antineoplastic chemotherapy induced anemia",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
